                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>The corundumite fires a beam of freezing blue light in a @Template[type:line|distance:60]. Any creature in the area takes @Damage[6d10[cold]|options:area-damage] damage and must attempt a @Check[reflex|dc:38|options:area-effect,damaging-effect,inflicts:immobilized,inflicts:petrified] save. The corundumite can't use Cold Ray on its next turn.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> No effect.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> Half damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> Full damage and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Immobilized] for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Full damage and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Petrified] for 1 round. While petrified, the creature is transformed into solid ice instead of stone and gains weakness 5 to fire.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
